'' A NON-CONST STRING TO A CONST STRING PARAMETER IS ONE TIER DOWN, as fbc scores a same-type
'' match whose CONST differs: below 'zstring ptr' and 'byref zstring', above the wide strings.
'' tiko-lang costed adding const as one step above exact, so offered { byref const string,
'' const zstring ptr } 'g( sv )' ran the const string body where fbc-modern runs the zstring
'' ptr one -- fb/hash.bi's 'HashOf( s )' is _ZN2FB6HASHOFEPKc under fbc (measured 2026-09-19);
'' the same for 'sv & "x"' and 'byref const zstring'. And a STRING reaching a ustring or a
'' wstring is fbc's half tier, dearer than a zstring ptr (k, q) and than a const string
'' passed to a byval one (p). { const string, const ustring } still takes the string (m).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/overload-const-string.bas
